---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/daniel-nowak.png';
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../data/site';
import { ui } from '../i18n';
const DISCLOSURE = ui('en').disclosure;
---
<Site
  title="About Daniel Nowak | DNA4Digital"
  description="Eighteen years of operations across hospitality, BPO and SaaS. #1 EMEA revenue team at Google Customer Solutions, RevOps at Sensay, client operations at SpotOn, Associate Partner at Yameo."
>
  <Panel rung={1} kicker="02 · About">
    <h1>Look at the handoffs before you buy another tool</h1>
    <Image src={portrait} alt="Daniel Nowak at his desk" width={300} class="photo" loading="eager" />
    <p class="lead">I'm Daniel Nowak. I fix the way revenue and operations run day to day, then apply AI where it pays back.</p>
    <p>I came to AI from operations: eighteen years of them, thirteen spent running restaurants, conference floors and hotel F&amp;B departments in Poland and Ireland. When a process breaks in a hotel restaurant, you have a room full of people waiting for their food, and you find out within the hour.</p>
    <p>Hospitality taught me to check the handoffs between people before blaming the tools, and that is still the work I sell. I do it independently through DNA4Digital, and as Associate Partner at Yameo, a Dutch-Polish enterprise software house, when a client needs the system built as well as designed.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div><b>#1</b><span>revenue team in EMEA, Google CS</span></div>
      <div><b>5&times;</b><span>funnel engagement, Sensay</span></div>
      <div><b>30%</b><span>less ticket handling time, SpotOn</span></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="mission">Why I do this</h2>
    <p>I moved into tech in 2021 and saw the same pattern from the inside that I'd watched from the kitchen pass: companies buying tools for problems that sat in the process. Drop a new tool into a messy process and you move the mess somewhere else, faster. I work in the opposite order: process first, then automation, then AI.</p>

    <h2 id="story">My story</h2>
    <p>I spent thirteen years in hospitality operations. I opened a café and bakery in Donegal National Park, ran four F&amp;B outlets serving 600 covers a day at the Royal Marine, and turned a hotel restaurant into a takeaway business in the first weeks of COVID using Facebook, Google Ads and a redrawn menu. Along the way I learned SOPs, forecasting, margin control, and what happens to a team when nobody is sure how the process works.</p>
    <p>In 2021 I joined TTEC as a Google Ads account manager. TTEC promoted me to POD Lead within four months, then to Team Leader running Google Customer Solutions for Poland and CZ/SK as a TTEC vendor partner. That team finished <strong>#1 for revenue in EMEA</strong>, and I took the Platinum Club award for best manager in the region. I also held a 5/5 employee satisfaction score for four straight quarters, and nobody left the team, which protected the margin.</p>
    <p>At Sensay, an AI SaaS company, I took on the technical side. I migrated legacy systems into HubSpot, enriched the data with Breeze Intelligence, engineered automated sequences in n8n and Zapier, and assembled Looker Studio dashboards that merged CRM, product and website analytics. <strong>Funnel engagement went up fivefold.</strong></p>
    <p>At SpotOn I ran client operations for a restaurant-tech platform. I audited the workflows, automated the right ones and rebuilt the SOPs so the answers were written down instead of living in people's heads. Together that <strong>cut ticket handling time by 30%</strong>. Having started in restaurants, I'd come full circle.</p>
    <p>I'm now Associate Partner at Yameo, a Dutch-Polish software house that has built enterprise systems for banking, insurance and healthcare since 2006. When the work I've mapped needs engineers, I have a team behind me that delivers on a fixed price, a fixed date and a signed SLA. Without that team, I could only hand you a plan.</p>

    <div class="pcards three">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Why work with me</h3><p>You get a plan you can read, quick pilots and results you can measure. The person who scopes the work with you is the person who delivers it.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>What I stand for</h3><p><strong>Simplicity:</strong> if you can't explain a process on one page, your team won't follow it. <strong>Accountability:</strong> I name the number, the baseline and the timeframe. <strong>Partnership:</strong> I teach only what I've run myself.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>The arc</h3><p>Hospitality taught me operations and Google taught me scale. At Sensay I learned to build the systems I used to specify, and with Yameo I can take on builds too big for one person.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="approach">How I work</h2>
    <p>From diagnosis to rollout, at a pace your team can absorb alongside its day job.</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><h3>Audit &amp; process map</h3><p>I map how work moves day to day, which rarely matches the org chart: bottlenecks, handoffs, duplicated fields and the workarounds people have built for themselves. You get the friction ranked by what it costs you.</p><a href="/services/#audit">More about audits &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><h3>Pilot &amp; training</h3><p>We test on live examples with your data, I train the people who'll run it, and we choose tools to fit the process.</p><a href="/services/#training">More about training &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><h3>Implementation &amp; scale</h3><p>I set up standards, SOPs, KPIs and dashboards so your team keeps the gains after I've gone.</p><a href="/services/#consulting">More about consulting &rarr;</a></li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="practice">Where I'm strongest</h2>
    <div class="pcards three">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Go-to-market &amp; RevOps</h3><p>Funnel and pipeline design, qualification rules, handoffs, CRM architecture and reporting. Intent-driven prospecting off ICP and persona mapping, A/B-tested outbound cadences that lifted engagement 18%, and a legacy stack migrated into one HubSpot instance with reports leadership could read.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Process architecture</h3><p>Mapping, standardisation, ownership, SOPs, KPIs and quality control. This is the Lean Six Sigma half of my work, and it decides whether anything else works. When a client brings me an &ldquo;AI problem&rdquo;, I usually find an undocumented process underneath.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>AI enablement &amp; automation</h3><p>Low-code architecture in n8n and Zapier, AI-enhanced training, internal troubleshooting chatbots, sales assistants and concierge bots. I also write the governance that tends to get skipped: SOPs, GDPR data-sharing agreements and analytics integrations that stand up to scrutiny.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="track-record">Where this experience comes from</h2>
    <p>I've worked eighteen years in operations across hospitality, BPO and SaaS, in Poland, Ireland and the wider EMEA region.</p>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li><b>Yameo, Associate Partner</b><span>Enterprise software delivery for banking, insurance, healthcare and the public sector.</span></li>
      <li><b>Google Customer Solutions, via TTEC</b><span>Led the PL and CZ/SK team as a TTEC vendor partner. #1 revenue team in EMEA; Platinum Club, Best Manager, Q3 2024.</span></li>
      <li><b>TTEC, Team Leader</b><span>EMEA business development. Enterprise BPO solutioning and C-level negotiation.</span></li>
      <li><b>Sensay, Senior Technical BDM</b><span>RevOps architecture and AI product deployment.</span></li>
      <li><b>SpotOn, Client Operations Manager</b><span>Workflow automation and operational enablement.</span></li>
      <li><b>Balkans Crypto, Sales Director</b><span>Commercial strategy for a 2,000-attendee Web3 conference; Tier-1 exchange and L1/L2 partnerships.</span></li>
      <li><b>Hospitality operations, 13 years</b><span>Restaurants, conference floors and hotel F&amp;B in Poland and Ireland.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>Credentials:</strong> Lean Six Sigma Black Belt &middot; Machine Learning with Python (V2) &middot; Web Development &middot; BA Economics (Wyższa Szkoła Finansów i Informatyki, 2026)</p>
    <p class="disclosure" id="disclosure">{DISCLOSURE} I raise this in our first conversation.</p>

    <h2>Find out where I'd start</h2>
    <p>In a free 30-minute call I'll tell you whether your first move should be an audit, a pilot, or writing down how the work is supposed to happen.</p>
    <div class="btnrow">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a consultation</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/services/">See services</a>
    </div>
  </Panel>
</Site>
